      "body": "## Overview\n\nAdd RedHatAI speculative-decoding modes to the Gemma 4 31B and GPT-OSS 120B recipes.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Adds the Gemma 4 DFlash2 and GPT-OSS EAGLE3 modes with checkpoint-specific token counts.\n- Keeps the existing default speculative-decoding selection unchanged where applicable.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidation is pending; this PR is intentionally a draft.\n\n- Passed: `git diff --check`.\n- Planned source validation (not run): from `/home/Roderick-Wu/recipes`, run `pnpm install` if dependencies are missing, then:\n  `node scripts/validate-source.mjs --source vllm --dir /home/Roderick-Wu/recipe-worktrees/other-speculators/recipes`\n- Planned serving smoke test (not run): run the generated H100-compatible command for each new mode on the 8xH100 node; check `/v1/models`, generate a short completion, and record speculative-token acceptance.\n\n## Details\n\nThe recipe descriptions record the versions and settings stated by the checkpoint cards without claiming new end-to-end results. AI assistance was used to prepare this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] Design Fit: confines changes to existing recipe files and preserves existing defaults.\n- [ ] Testing and Validation: pending author validation.\n- [x] Code Quality and Style: `git diff --check` passed.\n- [x] Pull Request Contents: includes checkpoint-specific constraints and a validation plan.\n</details>\n\n",
